cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MIRL Glean: images gathered from open collections"
abstract: >-
  A no-build, local-first tool that sends one search to twenty-two open museum,
  library, and archive collections at once (among them the Met, the Art
  Institute of Chicago, the Rijksmuseum, Yale, the Library of Congress,
  Europeana, Japan Search, and K-samsök) and returns one set of results with
  every licence read into a plain rights state. Picked images keep their
  records, Chicago citations, and a picks file the user holds; downloads come as
  a zip whose manifest records each file's sha-256, source, retrieval time, and
  rights. Thirty further collections with no open search API, among them JSTOR
  through a library proxy and archives of the Arab world, open with the same
  query. Arabic and right-to-left ready. Runs in the browser, no build.
